    lines += ['','Whole-helper native peaks: '+', '.join(f"#{t['technique_id']}: {t['performance']['process_peak_working_set_bytes']:,} bytes" for t in ts)+'. These include imports, all workloads and tracing; they are not per-workload or CLI-child peaks. Each resource record retains the environment, inputs, three untraced full-report runs, a separate traced run, and a full CLI call. These are observed local measurements, not universal guarantees.','','**Scientific meaning**','','These releases distinguish bounded software behavior, source-supported historical attribution, independently verified mathematical calculations, and synthetic simulations. All #55–#60 examples are synthetic. Software verification is not empirical proof of predictive validity. Historical symbolic systems and appearance references retain their attribution and assessment limits. No psychic, precognitive, clinical BCI, unidentified causal, live-market, weather-horizon or other-universe prediction is certified.','','#49 is a preserved retrospective evaluation on 288 pinned NOAA monthly CO₂ observations. Its validation-selected drift model scored test MAE **2.537249963267 ppm**, versus seasonal-naïve **2.1794 ppm** (ratio **1.164196551008**). It underperformed; the selected model was not replaced by the diagnostic test winner. The 300 overlapping test forecast cells cover 36 distinct target months and are not independent replications. Source-vintage certification remains false. This result does not establish general forecasting superiority.','','**Cross-engine compatibility**','','- #51 and #57 share binary Brier and two-category scoring conventions. Their question, participant, weighting and revision schemas remain separate.','- #51 resolution and #58 settlement require explicit identity, evidence and authority mapping. #51 permits dispute/void/correction histories; #58 settles binary play credits once. Forecast cutoff equality is eligible in #51/#57, while #58 trades and quotes must precede close.','- #52 carries deterministic PRNG and synthetic provenance. Correlated simulation runs cannot become empirical probabilities or independent samples merely by export. #60 uses exact editorial weights without RNG.','- #53 preserves measurement availability and refuses retroactive assimilation. Unknown targets are not scored. This is compatible in principle with forecasting chronology, but its update convention is distinct.','- #54 uses exact synchronous binary grid ticks; #59 uses approximate continuous RK4 steps. Both complete requested horizons, but their states, units and numerical conventions are not interchangeable.','- #56 interventional effects require its declared identification assumptions. Forecast and scenario conditional probabilities do not inherit causal meaning.','- #60 is a generic finite probability/utility representation, not a quantum-state or multiverse model.','','The [interface witnesses](future-interface-verification.json) check all seven boundaries. No production connector or unified orchestration framework was introduced.','','**Prioritized refinement**','','The [P1/P2 backlog](future-prioritized-refinement-backlog.json) preserves source-linked items for all 54 releases and groups them by practical value, correctness risk and effort: scientific validation; source access and rights; real datasets; advanced mathematics; historical variations; cross-engine integration; performance; optional UI/API/product work. These extensions remain deferred. No new runtime packages, paid APIs or live external services were added.','','**Commit traceability**','','| ID | Audit | Source/profile | Fixtures | Engine | CLI | Verification | Acceptance | Closure |','|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|']
